    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↓dose ICS–formoterol = the preferred reliever @ every step (prn in mild asthma; maintenance + reliever in mod–severe persistent); formoterol w an ICS may be dosed Q3–4 h by some protocols. ICS + LABA + LAMA (eg, fluticasone furoate/umeclidinium/vilanterol) for severe persistent asthma (step 5)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Oropharyngeal candidiasis. ↑ PNA risk in COPD (higher in pts > 65 y)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated as primary tx of status asthmaticus or acute asthma/COPD needing intensive measures; fluticasone/salmeterol DPI also in severe milk-protein allergy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, ritonavir, clarithromycin, itraconazole, ketoconazole): ⍉recommended (↑ systemic steroid and cardiovasc effects)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rising SABA use = deteriorating asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " reassess the regimen. In COPD, watch for PNA (its features overlap w exacerbations)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rinse mouth w H2O w.o swallowing after each use. Don't exceed the prescribed inhalations (mometasone/formoterol: ⍉more than two inhalations BID). Improvement can start w.in 15 min, but full benefit may take 2 wks or longer."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
